desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Use Defused Xmlrpc"
	title_zh: "Use Defused Xmlrpc"
	type: vuln
	level: high
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-use-defused-xmlrpc"
	risk: "xxe"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from rule `use-defused-xmlrpc` (python/lang/security/use-defused-xmlrpc.yaml).
Original message: Detected use of xmlrpc. xmlrpc is not inherently safe from vulnerabilities. Use defusedxml.xmlrpc instead.
CWE: CWE-776: Improper Restriction of Recursive Entity References in DTDs ('XML Entity Expansion')
References:
- https://pypi.org/project/defusedxml/
- https://docs.python.org/3/library/xml.html#xml-vulnerabilities
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.py": <<<POS
import xmlrpclib
POS
	"safefile://pos.py": <<<NEG
import defusedxmlrpc
NEG
)

${*.py}.pattern_regex(/(?:import\s+xmlrpclib)|(?:import\s+SimpleXMLRPCServer)|(?:import\s+xmlrpc)/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "high",
	title: "Use Defused Xmlrpc",
	title_zh: "Use Defused Xmlrpc",
	message: "Use Defused Xmlrpc detected.",
}
